.SH EXAMPLES
Evaluate a single command:
.IP
.EX
bashclient \-s /tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock \(rs
           \-a \(dq$(cat /tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock.token)\(dq \(rs
           \-e \(aqecho hello world\(aq
.EE
.PP
Run a script file:
.IP
.EX
bashclient \-s /tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock \(rs
           \-a \(dq$(cat /tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock.token)\(dq \(rs
           \-f setup.sh
.EE
.PP
Interactive session:
.IP
.EX
bashclient \-s /tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock \(rs
           \-a \(dq$(cat /tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock.token)\(dq \(rs
           \-i
.EE
.PP
Using a shell wrapper for convenience:
.IP
.EX
#!/bin/sh
SOCK=/tmp/bash\-server\-$(id \-u)/sock
TOKEN=$(cat \(dq${SOCK}.token\(dq)
exec bashclient \-s \(dq$SOCK\(dq \-a \(dq$TOKEN\(dq \(dq$\(at\(dq
.EE
